#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "0713e68d-2b3e-5010-954f-7891d96bdbbb" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3640" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-1$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $h(x)$ | $z(x)$ | $h'(x)$ | $z'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-1$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $6$ | $3$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right)$ at $x=-1$." :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\dfrac{h(x)}{z(x)}\\right) = \\dfrac{h'(x)z(x)-h(x)z'(x)}{(z(x))^2}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}((h(x))/(z(x))) \\mid _{x =-1} &= (h^{′}(-1)z(-1) - h(-1)z^{′}(-1))/((z(-1))^{2}) \\\\\n&= (6 \\cdot 2 - (-4) \\cdot 3)/(2^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{24}{4} \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100576 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of the Product or Quotient of a Composition of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "787e9681-8009-5ba8-acda-6d8830397d18" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3641" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, we have\n$f(1)=2, \\quad f'(1)=2, \\quad g(1)=-1, \\quad g'(1)=3$.\nIf $h(x) = \\left(f(x)-1 \\right)\\left(2g(x)+1\\right)$, compute $h'(1)$." :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big(uv\\Big) = u \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} +v \\dfrac{\\textrm du}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)-1$ and\n\n$$\nv=2g(x)+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = f'(x) \\qquad \\text{and}\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d v}{\\textrm d x} = 2g'(x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh^{′}(x) &= u\\frac{dv}{dx} + v\\frac{du}{dx} \\\\\n&= (f(x) - 1) \\cdot 2g^{′}(x) + (2g(x) + 1) \\cdot f^{′}(x) \\\\\n&= 2g^{′}(x)(f(x) - 1) + f^{′}(x)(2g(x) + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh^{′}(1) &= 2g^{′}(1)(f(1) - 1) + f^{′}(1)(2g(1) + 1) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot (2 - 1) + 2 \\cdot (2 \\cdot (-1) + 1) \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Linear Combination of Functions Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "a87386d5-4a1b-539c-aeb9-dd60181baa4f" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6154" :question/problem "The values of functions $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=-3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $p(x)$ | $q(x)$ | $p'(x)$ | $q'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $8$ | $0$ | $-2$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(p(x) + 5q(x) \\big)$ at $x=-3$." :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(p(x) + 5q(x) \\right) = p'(x) + 5q'(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(p(x) + 5q(x)) \\mid _{x =-3} &= p^{′}(-3) + 5q^{′}(-3) \\\\\n&= 0 + 5 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100664 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Product Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/id #uuid "d1d0a3ec-2a84-580a-968e-53b773510853" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-6155" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nCompute $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big)$ at $x=0$." :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\big(f(x)g(x)\\big) = f(x)g'(x)+f'(x)g(x)\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(f(x)g(x)) \\mid _{x = 0} &= f(0)g^{′}(0) + f^{′}(0)g(0) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot 0 + 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Quotient Given the Necessary Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b3509b-0364-5fa0-a6ea-1b6f4632a646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099697} {:answer/id #uuid "850438ad-51c9-5986-97ef-19a3e767ab64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099698} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe1259c-b6c0-5ac0-adc1-79e776472972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099699} {:answer/id #uuid "decde0ab-bebe-5a15-afa6-992f4cf7299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099700} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5a2d84-2b1d-51f3-b7b7-396e3ccef9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "decde0ab-bebe-5a15-afa6-992f4cf7299a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099700} :answer-field/id #uuid "750db73d-40a6-5399-8d52-2868fecc4fdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099696}] :question/id #uuid "3cd961da-21ad-5bfd-88cf-d61e5f8fe86e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48844" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you are given the following data:\n\n$f(0) = 2, f^{′}(0) = 2, g(0) = 1, g^{′}(0) = 2$\n\nCompute $\\frac{d}{dx}((f(x))/(g(x)))$ at $x = 0$."}]}
